==Evolution==
Evolves into '''The Southern Sun''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''The Southern Sunflare''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
As a variant of an [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOUL]], Kaguya of the Coast has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Kaguya of the Coast bears only negligible differences compare to [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|Princess Kaguya]], so the way to use her stays the same.

Her strength comes from being extremely cost efficient and hitting very often, to the point that she can't even be rushed down by a Doge Dark, who would instead be juggled back continuously. All this impressive offensive potential comes at the hefty price of a mediocre range for Ultra Souls standard as well as health so low that it's basically a one-hit kill against most enemies with adequate magnification for her level.

Dark and Alien enemies have a large selection of frontline units that Kaguya of the Coast may outrange, but Alien units tend to have barriers, few knockbacks, high health or high damage most of the time, making her rarely effective. She can, however, be used effectively against some enemies such as [[Nimoy Bore]] or [[Star Peng]]s, even in stages that cap the cost as 600, where she and her normal version are the only Ubers available. Darks are where she shines, as a couple hits can usually knock them back and keep them there, slowed, for a bit, thus relieving the frontline from the high pushing power that characterizes Dark enemies. She isn't as effective as the likes of [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]] in stalling tougher enemies, but that is also a thing she can be used for quite effectively.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Although with short uptime, the Southern Sun has a guaranteed slow and good stats, which make it less effective against hordes, but great against strong, longer ranged enemies against whom the Normal Form falls short, such as [[I.M. Phace]].

As a frail backliner with long attack windup, she is best suited for non-aggressive approaches with many meatshields or tanks, so it may stay safe in the background and land hits often.

For generalist usage, the Southern Sun is fairly standard, with everything being useable and quite good, but nothing being excellent. She should never be picked above a specialized generalist, but her lack of relevant downsides still makes her more useable than most for this.

==='''True Form'''===
The Southern Sunflare can now target Aku enemies. This would normally give her several new targets to slow, especially with her range advantage, but many Aku enemies are protected with a shield. Thankfully, this is why she also comes with a 50% chance to pierce those shields instantly. As her attack cycle is over 9 seconds, she would have to wait a good while before attacking again if she fails to pierce the shield straight away. However, if she does succeed, then she can seriously chunk her Aku targets, as her attacks would do almost 46k damage and slow Aku enemies for over 3 and a half seconds. Even if her attack doesn't instantly pierce a shield, it can still do around 46k damage at least to them. This is also made better with her ability to outrange serious threats such as [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Le'Behemoth]]. With a 50% chance to pierce shields per attack and over 9 seconds between hits, she does need to get lucky to make the most of her kit, but even with this luck factor, she is a good generalist.

